description:
FLAGGED s507p (perf round 39; #2111 M3 and #2115 (c)).  A scalar behind a private-buffer magic cell (:memfh = an open in-memory write handle; :strbuf = a string past 200 chars grown by .=) answers READS with a simple-string snapshot taken once after each write.  `length` reads the live buffer (no copy, s507p 85060938), but every OTHER reader -- a regex match, eq, substr, index, print of the scalar -- after each write copies the whole string, so a loop that writes and then matches is O(n) per iteration:

    my $buf = ""; open my $fh, ">", \$buf; for (1 .. N) { print $fh "line\n"; last if $buf =~ /STOP/ }
    our $g; for (1 .. N) { $g .= "x"; $n++ if $g =~ /xx$/ }

This is not worse than fee16466 for :strbuf (there every append itself copied); for :memfh it is the M3 cost (fee16466 had no copy, but shared the buffer = #2111's silent wrong).  Candidate: hand NON-RETAINING readers (match, eq, index, print) the live buffer the way length does -- each such reader must be shown not to keep its operand (a match keeps $& etc. -- do-regex-match already copies a non-simple subject; check what else).  Measure on probes/m3-bounded.pl-style shapes first.
